{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Existing companions could render small textured entities but could not receive a complete authored Scene or load the original catalog GLBs. This draft extends the existing ARKit/SceneKit and ARCore/Filament owners with negotiated v2 Scene delivery and authorized, integrity-checked model loading. V1 and the canonical Chronicle observation/progression path remain intact.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Reuse the original SC02 chest/compass, hierarchy, units, bottom pivot, material intent and revision identity; large model bytes use an authenticated asset endpoint outside the 16 KiB bridge.\n- Extend the existing native renderers, anchored updates, geometry selection, staged activation/cancellation and foreground cache/lifecycle handling. Unsupported capabilities retain Guided View.\n- Provide a browser graph presentation helper for the active provider's future integration. Browser AR/Crossdeck integration remains pending.\n- Prepare an isolated synthetic laptop preview, explain native local-network permission, and repair browser account submission, Guided text contrast and the persistent mobile Close control.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Shared/native/asset/browser graph regressions: 125 passes across 11 files; account lifecycle: 12 passes. Android JVM boundaries: 167 v1 and 45 v2 assertions. Full TypeScript, focused lint, both APK builds and documentation/feature checks passed at their source-bound checkpoints.\n- Android source `c2357ffe` passed ordinary [run 38833266576](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/38833266576): 16/16 tests, actual production GPU hits for both authored model entities, two background misses and two cleared-scene misses. Four original PNGs, raw digests, transforms/materials, disposal and canonical real-SQLite scenario passed independent review. Maximum callback/publication times were 4.815/5.007 seconds within the original per-frame 10-second limit. Ordinary SWANGLE emulator proof; cleared alpha>16 counts are zero but the PNGs retain alpha-one pixels.\n- iOS raster source `aecbf27d` passed [38819289805](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/38819289805): 24 passes, no failures, one expected skip. Six original Simulator Metal/SceneKit frames show chest 0/8,301/0 and compass 0/2,509/0 visible pixels, correct original geometry/materials/transforms and cleanup, within the single 20-second deadline. Canonical scenario and independent artifact/source review passed.\n- New iOS fixture source `2f2d55fd` failed [38838018116](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/38838018116): 23 passes, one failure and one expected skip. Its first opaque readback point returned no geometry hit while the transparent vertical mirror hit. The exact failed receipt, two original chest frames and cleanup are preserved. A bounded fixture-only fixed-Y conversion is source `9314c749`; original assertions, six frames and the single 20-second deadline remain. No geometry-selection pass is claimed for the earlier failed source.\n- Corrected iOS source `9314c749` compiled and passed all four NCL methods in [38840109053](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/38840109053): six original frames, actual nearest mesh hits mapped to distinct authored IDs, fixed query/world-to-viewport/inverse-pixel roundtrips, mirror/background/removed-graph misses and cleanup passed. Sealing finished in 2.196 seconds; maximum roundtrip error was 0.00003815 pixels. Overall result remains FAILURE (23/1/1): the unchanged Home/background lifecycle assertion failed and the canonical scenario did not run. Independent review verified the exact evidence and retained the unknown cause. ONE unchanged-candidate [replay 38841961822](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/actions/runs/38841961822), with the identical generated transport tree and no changed assertion/timeout/profile/backend, passed 24 tests with zero failures and one exact expected skip. All four NCL methods, six fresh frames, actual mesh/entity/projection/miss checks, canonical real-SQLite zero progression and all cleanup passed; sealing finished in 2.113 seconds within the original 20-second deadline. Final independent review verified all 23 published entries and original XCTest database, and all 106 preceding iOS files remain byte-exact. The earlier Home failure remains preserved with an unknown cause; no lifecycle repair or physical acceptance is inferred.\n- Actual authenticated desktop/emulated-mobile Guided Inspect matched persisted observations without progression, with asset integrity and close/reopen proof. Independent rendered review passed; original captures and sanitized traces remain source-bound supporting evidence.\n- Restored laptop preview at `https://192.168.0.18:8449` after a guarded LAN rebind: two HTTP bootstrap and three normally verified HTTPS restore checks, plus 11 fresh authenticated asset checks. Same CA/keys/profile/expiry and canonical synthetic Scene/Voyage were retained; only the probe's own new session was revoked. No global trust or firewall changes; phone reachability is owner-deferred.\n- Full runtime source and all new Git metadata are on task-owned D: locations. Complete relocation digests and original evidence are preserved. Automatic approval review blocked removal of the inactive verified C: duplicate; it remains intact and no disk recovery is claimed.\n\n- Final local publication checks passed: private-value scan across 850 files/archive entries, formatting, 1,923 indexed engineering records / 3,176 documentation paths and documentation validation. Feature synchronization/validation passed with 68 entries; the generated catalog is byte-identical and no capability is promoted. New Git mutations and staged-byte checks use only the task-owned D: clone.\n\n## Held acceptance\n\nThe initial vertical slice and full mission remain incomplete. The final 03:07 UTC immutable-source audit found protected main at `f935ab3e` and owner PR #721 at `6dcabd54`, still draft and unmerged. Registry bytes are unchanged: main lacks the required `crossdeck.phase2.continuity` design, and both exact heads lack the browser adapter. No final Sounding Line qualification or merge has been attempted.\n\nA signed iPhone installation, physical ARKit/ARCore anchoring and recovery, native Inspect/continuity, actual-device performance/thermal measurements and owner acceptance remain pending. No physical Android device is available. Software, emulator, Guided browser and Node TLS proof do not establish these results. Richer effects, occlusion, scanning and shared anchors remain subsequent validated increments.\n\nFailed attempts and their original source identities are retained in the NCL-01 engineering record. Feature Catalog: NO CHANGE REQUIRED\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T20:00:58Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T20:00:58Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"feat(parallax): add shared scene delivery and native GLB rendering slice","oid":"bfb27c63727ee217761bfd1b296e43bdc117f25d"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T20:15:12Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T20:15:12Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix(parallax): disambiguate iOS entity pose variable","oid":"e25c0ee59fc7331bd66648549d968ff98f99b02a"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T20:28:01Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T20:28:01Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix(auth): keep early account submissions out of request URLs","oid":"90ceacb60a9306bc187620620c85de3be85fa880"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T20:32:53Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T20:32:53Z","messageBo